{"id":1369,"date":"2020-11-27T15:13:11","date_gmt":"2020-11-27T23:13:11","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1369"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:35","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:35","slug":"program-the-viking-ship-robot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-viking-ship-robot\/","title":{"rendered":"Program the Viking Ship Robot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165b0a690\" name=\"6a22165b0a690\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What does it do?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The Viking Ship Bot is programmed so that the left and right sensors check for objects. If they do, the bot will swing towards the object. If the Viking Ship Bot has swung back and forth for a hundred times, it will play a song!<\/p>\n<p>This is the\u00a0Viking Ship Bot&#8217;s pseudocode:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check the left and right sensors.<\/li>\n<li>If the left sensor senses an object, swing to the left.<\/li>\n<li>If the right sensor senses an object, swing to the right.<\/li>\n<li>If the Viking Ship Bot has swung a hundred times, play a melody.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165b0a7b4\" name=\"6a22165b0a7b4\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Setup<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The first thing you need to do is include the Smart Inventor library at the top of your code. Next, in void setup(), include your motors.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n \r\nvoid setup() {\r\n\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>Next, set up variables for your left and right IR sensors, and use\u00a0those\u00a0variables\u00a0in\u00a0void setup()\u00a0so the\u00a0sensors\u00a0will know if they&#8217;re seeing a\u00a0value\u00a0that isn&#8217;t normal. Add a buffer of 50 to leave some room for error.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n\r\n \r\nint baseLevelLeft = 0;\r\nint baseLevelRight = 0;\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\nvoid setup() {\r\n\r\n  SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n\r\n  baseLevelLeft = analogRead(19) - 50;\r\n  baseLevelRight = analogRead(21) - 50;\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165b0a810\" name=\"6a22165b0a810\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add sensors<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In\u00a0void loop(), set\u00a0variables\u00a0for each\u00a0sensor\u00a0so that they get and save the\u00a0value\u00a0that is being read from their corresponding\u00a0pin.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt; \r\n\r\nint baseLevelLeft = 0;\r\nint baseLevelRight = 0;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n\r\n SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n\r\n baseLevelLeft = analogRead(19) - 50;\r\n baseLevelRight = analogRead(21) - 50;\r\n}\r\n\r\n void loop() {\r\n int leftSensor = analogRead(19);\r\n int rightSensor = analogRead(21);\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165b0a879\" name=\"6a22165b0a879\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add if statements<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Time for the main section of the code! You need to use an if statement to check if one of the sensors has detected an object.<\/p>\n<p>Unlike the amusement park ride the Viking Ship Bot is modeled after, the Viking Ship Bot cannot swing up and around &#8212; it can only swing in the opposite direction of the last direction it went. To keep track of the last direction, you can create a variable named lastDirection in void setup() and then use it in void loop(). This will be updated when the code runs.<\/p>\n<p>To count how many times the Viking Ship Bot has swung, create a variable named successCount, and then in void loop(), add += 1 to it. This will add 1 to the counter every time the bot swings back and forth.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint baseLevelLeft = 0;\r\nint baseLevelRight = 0;\r\nint Right = 0;\r\nint Left = 1;\r\nint lastDirection = Right;\r\nint successCount = 0;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n\r\n  SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n\r\n  baseLevelLeft = analogRead(19) - 50;\r\n  baseLevelRight = analogRead(21) - 50;\r\n}\r\n\r\n \r\nvoid loop() {\r\n\r\n  int leftSensor = analogRead(19);\r\n  int rightSensor = analogRead(21);\r\n \r\n  if(leftSensor &lt; baseLevelLeft)\r\n  {\r\n    if(lastDirection == Right)\r\n    {\r\n      lastDirection = Left;\r\n      SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 100);\r\n      delay(75);\r\n      SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0);\r\n      successCount += 1;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  else if(rightSensor &lt; baseLevelRight)\r\n  {\r\n    if(lastDirection == Left)\r\n    {\r\n      lastDirection = Right;\r\n      SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 100);\r\n      delay(75);\r\n      SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0);\r\n      successCount += 1;\r\n    }\r\n  }<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165b0a8d0\" name=\"6a22165b0a8d0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add sound<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If the Viking Ship Bot has swung back and forth a hundred times, it will play a song! To do this, use the SmartInventor.Buzz command, which will play a note for a certain amount of time. We used 6 in our example, which means 1\/6 of a second. You will also need to include a command to set your success count back to zero.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n\r\n  int leftSensor = analogRead(19);\r\n  int rightSensor = analogRead(21);\r\n \r\n  if(leftSensor &lt; baseLevelLeft)\r\n  {\r\n    if(lastDirection == Right)\r\n    {\r\n      lastDirection = Left;\r\n      SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 100);\r\n      delay(75);\r\n      SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0);\r\n      successCount += 1;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  else if(rightSensor &lt; baseLevelRight)\r\n  {\r\n    if(lastDirection == Left)\r\n    {\r\n      lastDirection = Right;\r\n      SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 100);\r\n      delay(75);\r\n      SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0);\r\n      successCount += 1;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if(successCount &gt; 100)\r\n  {\r\n    successCount = 0;\r\n    SmartInventor.Buzz(NOTE_C5, 6);\r\n    SmartInventor.Buzz(NOTE_E5, 6);\r\n    SmartInventor.Buzz(NOTE_G5, 6);\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165b0a921\" name=\"6a22165b0a921\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Your final code should look something like this:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint baseLevelLeft = 0;\r\nint baseLevelRight = 0;\r\nint Right = 0;\r\nint Left = 1;\r\nint lastDirection = Right;\r\nint successCount = 0;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {  \r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();  \r\n    \r\n    baseLevelLeft = analogRead(19) - 50;  \r\n    baseLevelRight = analogRead(21) - 50;\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop() {  \r\n    int leftSensor = analogRead(19);  \r\n    int rightSensor = analogRead(21);   \r\n\r\n    if(leftSensor &lt; baseLevelLeft)  \r\n    {    \r\n        if(lastDirection == Right)    \r\n        {      \r\n            lastDirection = Left;      \r\n        \r\n            SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 100);      \r\n            delay(75);      \r\n            SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0);      \r\n\r\n            successCount += 1;    \r\n        }  \r\n    }  \r\n\r\n    else if(rightSensor &lt; baseLevelRight)  \r\n    {    \r\n        if(lastDirection == Left)    \r\n        {      \r\n            lastDirection = Right;      \r\n\r\n            SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 100);      \r\n            delay(75);      \r\n            SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0);      \r\n\r\n            successCount += 1;    \r\n        }  \r\n    }\r\n\r\n  if(successCount &gt; 100)\r\n  {\r\n    successCount = 0;\r\n    SmartInventor.Buzz(NOTE_C5, 6);\r\n    SmartInventor.Buzz(NOTE_E5, 6);\r\n    SmartInventor.Buzz(NOTE_G5, 6);\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165b0a964\" name=\"6a22165b0a964\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Still need help with the code or need to make sure your program is correct? Watch the video![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=GJms-dyN_f8&#8243; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 8 What does it do? [vc_column_text]The Viking Ship Bot is programmed so that the left and right sensors check for objects. If they do, the bot will swing&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-viking-ship-robot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":fals